    "code": " import math\n\nx, y, z = map(int, input().split())\n\na, b, c = map(int, input().split())\n\ns, rs, ls = map(int, input().split())\n\ndef can_win(ss):\n\n    for i in range(0, 205, 1):\n\n        for j in range(0, 105, 1):\n\n            if i * rs + j * ls <= ss:\n\n                q = y + i\n\n                p = z + j\n\n                pq = x + ((ss - i * rs - j * ls) // s)\n\n                an1 = 1000000000000.0\n\n                an2 = 1000000000000.0\n\n                if b - p > 0:\n\n                    an1 = math.ceil(pq / (b - p))\n\n                if q - c > 0:\n\n                    an2 = math.ceil(a / (q - c))\n\n                if (q > c and p >= b) or an1 > an2:\n\n                    return True\n\n    return False\n\nst = 0\n\nen = 100000\n\nwhile st <= en:\n\n    mid = (st + en) // 2\n\n    if can_win(mid):\n\n        en = mid - 1\n\n    else:\n\n        st = mid + 1\n\nprint(en + 1)",
